    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the speed-oriented upside of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands the highest score of the day (69.33) despite facing a lefty. His lead-off placement and park factors mitigate the platoon disadvantage, making him an essential start. **Casey Schmitt** also presents as a top-tier play (63.92); his dynamic platoon advantage against Lorenzen (+11%) and favorable spot in the order make him a high-efficiency engine for our run production. While **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a tougher path than his 61.40 score suggests, his matchup against a high-xERA starter (M\u00e1rquez, 5.58) provides the best \"pitcher-skill\" ceiling increase (+19%) on the roster, positioning him to capitalize on mistakes in the middle of the order.\n\nNavigating the bench required a disciplined approach to our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Carson Benge** was the most difficult exclusion, finishing just outside the starting nine with a 43.14 score. While his base projection was respectable, the combination of a platoon disadvantage and the superior efficiency offered by **Junior Caminero**\u2014whose 58.35 score remains rock-solid against Hancock\u2014pushed **Carson Benge** to the pine. Conversely, we remain cautious regarding the risks posed by elite arms; **Christian Yelich** faces a stiff test against Skenes, and both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are staring down the elite efficiency of Skubal. Despite these significant SP skill penalties, their high-leverage order placements preserve their status as recommended starts. Managers should monitor weather alerts for any late-breaking wind shifts that could further dampen the prospects of those facing the tougher lefties today.",
